Comment: 0,0:02:10.35,0:02:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{=88}Maesawa Beef Conditions
Dialogue: 1,0:02:10.35,0:02:19.26,Signs,,0,0,0,,{\q2\fnDelaGothic Bold\an2\fs23\frx6\fry0\blur0.7\org(427,167)\move(427,590,427,160)\clip(0,0,853,169)}Maesawa Beef refers to beef derived from cattle\Nproduced by individuals or businesses with a registered\Naddress in Maesawa in Oshu, Iwate, which were raised\Nin regions sharing natural environmental factors and sold through\Nthe Iwate Furusato Agricultural Cooperative Assocation,\Nprovided that it satisfies the following criteria:\N\N1. The cattle is of the Japanese Black breed;\N\N2. The cattle's place of birth can be verified using a calf registration\Ncertificate issued by the Wagyu Registry Association,\Nan equivalent certificate, etc.;\N\N3. For the cattle's fattening period: it must be bred by the producer\Nfor one year or longer, and it must spend the longest and final portions\Nof its breeding period within the aforementioned area of production;\N\N4. In compliance with The Law for Special Measures Concerning the\NManagement and Relay of Information for Individual Identification\Nof Cattle (commonly known as the Beef Traceability Law),\Nproducers must maintain records on the introduction of feeder cattle\Nand the status of their breeding and management for verification purposes;\N\N5. For carcass grading standards: per the Japan Meat Grading Association,\Nits meat quality grade must be 4 or higher, and its yield grade must be A or B.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.35,0:02:19.26,Signs,,0,0,0,,{=89}{\q2\fnDelaGothic Bold\an2\fs23\frx6\fry0\org(427,167)\move(427,590,427,160)\blur3\1a&HFE&\3a&HFE&\shad0.01\bord2\4c&H000000&\4a&H00&\clip(0,0,853,169)}Maesawa Beef refers to beef derived from cattle\Nproduced by individuals or businesses with a registered\Naddress in Maesawa in Oshu, Iwate, which were raised\Nin regions sharing natural environmental factors and sold through\Nthe Iwate Furusato Agricultural Cooperative Assocation,\Nprovided that it satisfies the following criteria:\N\N1. The cattle is of the Japanese Black breed;\N\N2. The cattle's place of birth can be verified using a calf registration\Ncertificate issued by the Wagyu Registry Association,\Nan equivalent certificate, etc.;\N\N3. For the cattle's fattening period: it must be bred by the producer\Nfor one year or longer, and it must spend the longest and final portions\Nof its breeding period within the aforementioned area of production;\N\N4. In compliance with The Law for Special Measures Concerning the\NManagement and Relay of Information for Individual Identification\Nof Cattle (commonly known as the Beef Traceability Law),\Nproducers must maintain records on the introduction of feeder cattle\Nand the status of their breeding and management for verification purposes;\N\N5. For carcass grading standards: per the Japan Meat Grading Association,\Nits meat quality grade must be 4 or higher, and its yield grade must be A or B.
